   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin-bottom:16px;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&#39;Segoe UI&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&#39;Apple Color Emoji&#39;,&#39;Segoe UI Emoji&#39;,&#39;Segoe UI Symbol&#39;;font-size:14px\">Hello.<br style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">I&#39;m trying to make my own function which is similar to cut_number but I cant understand what actually &#39;breaks&#39; is and how it works.<br style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">Could you please explain or provide some reference? Thx.</p><pre style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:11.899999618530273px;line-height:1.45;word-wrap:normal;padding:16px;overflow:auto;background-color:rgb(247,247,247);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;color:rgb(51,51,51)\"><code style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;background-color:transparent;border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;word-break:normal;display:inline;overflow:visible;line-height:inherit;word-wrap:normal\">cut_number &lt;- function(x, n = NULL, ...) {\r\n  brk &lt;- breaks(x, &quot;n&quot;, n)\r\n  if (anyDuplicated(brk))\r\n    stop(&quot;Insufficient data values to produce &quot;, n, &quot; bins.&quot;, call. = FALSE)\r\n  cut(x, brk , include.lowest = TRUE, ...)\r\n}</code></pre></div>"
    ]
   ]
